ads_prepare_changes:
## ads_prepare_changes

STEP 1 of changing ads yourself: validate a list of changes you authored and get a one-time write plan. changes_json is a JSON array; each item has a 'kind' plus its fields. Creating (Sponsored Products and Sponsored Display; pass family='sd' for SD): create_campaign, create_ad_group, create_product_ad, create_keyword (SP only — SD has no keywords; match_type BROAD/PHRASE/EXACT, default EXACT), create_target (SP takes asin; SD takes expression_json for product/views/audience targeting) — link them in one batch with 'ref' on a parent and 'campaign_ref'/'ad_group_ref' on children, in any order. Sponsored Brands cannot be created here (brand registry plus moderated creative). Changing (SP, and SB/SD for budget and state): set_bid, set_budget, set_placement, set_campaign_state, set_ad_group_state, set_keyword_state; pass family='sb'|'sd' for those campaigns. Negatives: add_negative_keyword (campaign_id, keyword_text, match_type EXACT|PHRASE default EXACT) and add_negative_target (campaign_id, asin). SP: with ad_group_id = ad-group level, without = campaign level. SB (family='sb'): both, ad_group_id required. SD (family='sd'): add_negative_target only, ad_group_id required — SD has no keywords, so no negative keywords. State is ENABLED or PAUSED — archiving is not offered because Amazon cannot undo it. New campaigns are created PAUSED unless you pass state explicitly. Max 50 changes. Nothing is written; you get the parsed plan back to show the seller. Free.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "changes_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "store_scope": {
      "description": "which store this call targets — an id from meta_list_stores. This tool takes an ads_profile id. Omit only when the account has a single store of that kind.",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "store_scope",
    "changes_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

