listing_prepare_change:
## listing_prepare_change

STEP 1 of changing or creating a listing over MCP: run Amazon's FULL server-side validation (VALIDATION_PREVIEW — nothing is written) on a listing payload you constructed, and get a one-time write plan when it passes. operation='put' creates/fully replaces (attributes_json = the complete attributes object per catalog_get_product_type); operation='patch' partially updates (patches_json = JSON Patch array, e.g. [{"op":"replace","path":"/attributes/item_name","value":[...]}]). For a VARIATION FAMILY (父子/变体) pass items_json instead: a JSON array [{sku, operation, attributes|patches}, ...] — parent SKU with parentage_level+variation_theme and no offer, each child with child_parent_sku_relationship and its axis attributes; every item is validated, cross-SKU consistency is linted, and ONE plan (one confirmation) covers the whole family. Returns Amazon's issues; a plan_id is only created when there are no ERROR-severity issues. Free.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "attributes_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "items_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "marketplace_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "operation": {
      "type": "string"
