restock_confirm_delivery_window:
## restock_confirm_delivery_window

Confirm the seller-chosen delivery window for ONE shipment (confirmDeliveryWindowOptions). Free. Re-validates against live options (gone, BLOCKED or past valid_until are refused). After confirming, Amazon no longer generates new window options for that shipment, but the chosen window can still be changed until the shipment closes — call again with another id. Only pass a window the seller picked.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "delivery_window_option_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "draft_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "shipment_id": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "draft_id",
    "shipment_id",
    "delivery_window_option_id"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_confirm_packing:
## restock_confirm_packing

STEP 3 — confirm a packing option and submit the box details. ONE BOX MAY CONTAIN SEVERAL MSKUs: pass items[] per box in boxes_json, e.g. {box_count:1, dimensions:{length:50,width:45,height:45,unit:'CM'}, weight:{value:9.6,unit:'KG'}, items:[{msku:'A',quantity:7},{msku:'B',quantity:5}]} — dimensions, weight and quantities are PER box. The legacy per-MSKU shape {msku, units_per_box, box_count, length, width, height, weight} still works (IN/LB) but cannot express mixed boxes; never put both shapes in one entry. Every MSKU in a box must belong to the same Amazon packing group. Expiry-based box splitting is not supported. Idempotent retry: if this draft already confirmed the SAME packing_option_id, the confirm is skipped and only the box details are (re)submitted; a DIFFERENT id returns packing_option_conflict. Across all boxes the per-MSKU totals must equal the plan's quantities exactly — over- and under-packing both reject the whole call.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "boxes_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "draft_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "packing_option_id": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "draft_id",
    "packing_option_id",
    "boxes_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

