restock_preview_shipment:
## restock_preview_shipment

Dry-run a shipment before anything is created on Amazon: validates the selected restock rows into MSKUs and, when boxes_json is given, checks the packing plan and returns the REAL physical box count. A box may hold SEVERAL MSKUs — pass items[] per box for mixed boxes. boxes_json is a JSON array; each entry is {box_count, dimensions:{length,width,height,unit:IN|CM}, weight:{value,unit:LB|KG}, items:[{msku,quantity}], client_box_ids?:[...]} where dimensions, weight and item quantities are PER physical box. Without boxes_json the box count is only a per-SKU estimate (box_count_source=ESTIMATED_SINGLE_SKU) and must not be used for quoting. Writes nothing to Amazon; it does one read-only lookup of each MSKU's prep/label owner so the preview shows the SAME prepOwner/labelOwner the create will submit (owners_resolved=false means Amazon could not be reached and the shown values are defaults). Rows are {style, color, size, quantity}; for dated goods (food, cosmetics, supplements…) add expiration (YYYY-MM-DD) and optionally manufacturing_lot_code per row — one expiration per SKU per plan (Amazon rule; different dates need separate plans). marketplace: optional site (US/CA/MX/UK/DE/JP… or a marketplace id); default is the store's own marketplace.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "boxes_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "marketplace": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "rows_json": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "rows_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_query_plan:
## restock_query_plan

Query the full restock plan rows (every SKU, all velocity windows, in-transit, suggested quantity, and the per-row calculation explanation) with a text filter and pagination. only_restock=True keeps rows with a suggestion > 0; include_explain=False trims the calculation steps for lighter pages. Feed next_cursor back to page. Stores selling in several marketplaces get one plan per inventory pool: pool='EU' (Pan-EU countries combined), 'UK', 'US', 'CA'…, or a country code ('DE') for that country alone; empty = the store's main pool. The response names the pool and lists the store's pools.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "cursor": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "include_explain": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "only_restock": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "page_size": {
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "pool": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "query": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_rename_shipment:
## restock_rename_shipment

Rename an inbound plan (default) or one of its shipments (shipment_id) on Amazon — e.g. to match the seller's PO or batch number. 1–100 characters. Free.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "draft_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "shipment_id": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "draft_id",
    "name"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_set_inbound_settings:
## restock_set_inbound_settings

Fix FBA inbound prerequisites without the web 后台. patch_json is a JSON object with any of: source_address (required: name/addressLine1/city/postalCode/countryCode/phoneNumber, plus stateOrProvinceCode for US/CA/AU/MX/BR/IN/CN/JP; optional addressLine2/companyName/email/districtOrCounty — incomplete address is rejected listing what's missing), contact {name, phoneNumber, email}, packing_specs [{style_code, box_qty, carton_length_in, carton_width_in, carton_height_in, carton_weight_lb}] and sku_mappings [{asin, seller_sku, style_code, color, size}]. Spec/mapping rows UPSERT by style_code/asin (rows not mentioned stay; max 200 per call). Writes only 粒粒's own database, never Amazon.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "patch_json": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "patch_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_set_item_compliance:
## restock_set_item_compliance

Set India (IN) inbound compliance per SKU (updateItemComplianceDetails — Amazon only uses it for IN). details_json: [{msku, hsn_code?, declared_value?: {amount, currency}, tax_rates?: [{tax_type: CGST|SGST|IGST|TOTAL_TAX, gst_rate?, cess_rate?}]}] (≤100). Values must come from the seller's tax records — never guess.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "details_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "marketplace": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "details_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_set_prep_details:
## restock_set_prep_details

Set each MSKU's FBA prep classification on Amazon (setPrepDetails). Needed when preview returns prep_classification_missing or creating a plan fails with FBA_INB_0182: prep set only in Seller Central is invisible to the API (category UNKNOWN). details_json: JSON array of {msku, prep_category, prep_types}. prep_category: NONE (no prep — prep_types defaults to [ITEM_NO_PREP]) / ADULT / BABY / FRAGILE / GRANULAR / HANGER / LIQUID / PERFORATED / SET / SHARP / SMALL / TEXTILE; other categories need at least one prep_type (ITEM_POLYBAGGING, ITEM_BUBBLEWRAP, ITEM_BOXING, ITEM_TAPING, ITEM_SETCREAT, ...). The classification MUST come from the seller — never guess; list the SKUs with the values you will send and get the seller's confirmation first. Writes the seller's catalog prep setting on Amazon for this marketplace (free, can be changed by calling again; it decides who preps/labels). Max 100 SKUs; invalid rows reject the whole batch before anything is sent. Returns what Amazon now stores per SKU plus the prep/label owners a plan will use.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "details_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "marketplace": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "details_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_set_shipment_tracking:
## restock_set_shipment_tracking

Report own-carrier tracking for one shipment after the carrier picks it up (updateShipmentTrackingDetails) — required for USE_YOUR_OWN_CARRIER shipments, so Amazon can match the arrival. tracking_json: small parcel → JSON array of tracking numbers in box order (one per box, count must equal the shipment's boxes) or [{box_id, tracking_id}]; freight (LTL/FTL) → {freight_bill_number (PRO, string or array), bill_of_lading_number?}. Partnered-carrier shipments are tracked by Amazon automatically (refused). Can be called again to correct numbers.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "draft_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "shipment_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "tracking_json": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "draft_id",
    "shipment_id",
    "tracking_json"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

restock_update_source_address:
## restock_update_source_address

Change where a shipment ships FROM (updateShipmentSourceAddress) — e.g. goods moved to another warehouse or forwarder. Only BEFORE the carrier is confirmed (Amazon rule). address_json: {name, addressLine1, addressLine2?, city, stateOrProvinceCode (US/CA/AU/MX/BR/IN/CN/JP), postalCode, countryCode, phoneNumber, companyName?, email?, districtOrCounty?}; omit to use the current inbound settings address. shipment_id narrows to one shipment (default all). Amazon invalidates existing carrier options — regenerate them with restock_get_transportation_options (next_action says so) and re-show quotes, which may change.

### 输入参数（JSON Schema）

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "address_json": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "draft_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "shipment_id": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "draft_id"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```
